UID:occ-venus-2026-09-14-mount-abu@occult.alokm.com
DTSTAMP:20260914T034332Z
DTSTART:20260914T114644Z
DTEND:20260914T122254Z
SUMMARY:The Moon occults Venus
DESCRIPTION:Venus disappears at 17:23:02 and reappears at 17:46:57 IST\, se
 en from Mount Abu.\nThe Moon is 35° up in the SW · daylight\, Sun +18°.
 \nTimes against the real lunar limb.\nMap\, timings and the view at the Mo
 on's edge: https://occult.alokm.com/venus-2026-09-14?city=Mount%20Abu
URL:https://occult.alokm.com/venus-2026-09-14?city=Mount%20Abu
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:The Moon occults Venus
TRIGGER:-PT30M
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ast-2026-09-28-1-ceres-708160-mount-abu@occult.alokm.com
DTSTAMP:20260916T024622Z
DTSTART:20260928T230829Z
DTEND:20260928T231829Z
SUMMARY:(1) Ceres hides a mag 11.8 star
DESCRIPTION:(1) Ceres hides a magnitude 11.8 star\, seen from Mount Abu.\nY
 ou are inside the path\, 65 km from its centre line: the star vanishes for
  up to 42.6 s.\nClosest approach 04:43:29 IST\, give or take 1 s. The star
  is 55° up in the E · dark sky.\nIt fades 0.1 magnitudes for up to 42.3 
 s on the centre line\, and the path is 939 km wide\, give or take 19 km.\n
 Finder chart\, the map and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/aster
 oids-2026-09#2026-09-28-1-ceres-708160
URL:https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2026-09#2026-09-28-1-ceres-708160
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
